1.1.text:
Article 46

To anticipate and prevent acts of violence against Women, the Regional Government shall undertake the following efforts:
a. b. f. providing various public facilities suitable for Women in public spaces;

developing an integrated information system database on acts of violence against Women;

strengthening the competence of apparatus handling violence against Women;

creating various modules and guidelines on prevention and handling of acts of violence against Women;

conducting various trainings and guidance for social workers engaged in organizations/institutions handling violence against Women;

inviting the community to play an active role in recovery and reintegration;

strengthening the function of community organizations engaged in the field of Women's empowerment; conducting various socializations regarding prevention and anticipation of acts of violence against Women to various community components in the Region; and optimizing the role of religious institutions, customary institutions, culture, as well as exploring local wisdom in order to prevent and minimize violence against Women both occurring at home or outside the home.

Article 44

The Regional Government in its efforts to protect Women as referred to in Article 42 is responsible for doing the following:
a. planning, making, establishing and organizing policies, programs and activities for the protection of Women;

strengthening and developing institutions providing Women's protection services;

conducting various preventive efforts early on so that violence against Women does not occur or can be minimized;

massively and continuously conducting various efforts so that acts of violence against Women do not occur in all fields of life;

massively and continuously preventing the occurrence of trafficking in persons (TPPO); and
f. continuously striving to provide protection for Women workers.

Article 10

Every Woman has the following rights:

a. to live in prosperous conditions physically and mentally;

b. to live in a family within a legal marriage bond in accordance with the teachings of the religion she adheres to;

f. to obtain education and teaching in all types, levels and pathways of education;

to obtain protection from discriminatory acts;

to obtain protection from economic and sexual exploitation;

to obtain protection from physical, psychological, sexual violence, and neglect;

to obtain decent work based on ability, interest and talent while upholding all matters related to her human nature;

to obtain access in advancing the business she runs in order to create adequate income improvement;

to obtain work leave while receiving wages/income in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations;

to receive special protection in the performance of work or profession against matters that may threaten safety and/or health related to the reproductive function of Women,

k. to obtain legal information and services according to her needs;
13- to enjoy a good and healthy environment in accordance with the standards and provisions of laws and regulations;

to own and manage joint property in a legal marriage in accordance with laws and regulations; and to have other rights attached in accordance with her human dignity based on the provisions of laws and regulations.

Article 198

Every parent in whose home there are Women, has a role in the following matters:
a. providing equal and comparable opportunities to Women in terms of obtaining access and opportunities to pursue education at all levels;

preventing every Woman who is part of the family members under their leadership from receiving arbitrary, harsh, and inhumane treatment; protecting their family members who are Women so that they do not experience pressure and sexual harassment, physical and psychological violence that causes the Women concerned to be unable to live their lives properly;

preventing a female family member from entering into early marriage below the age limit determined by Law; and not forcing a female family member to marry a man/male whom she does not desire.

Article 23

In order to implement the objective of providing protection of Women's rights from various forms of violence and other discriminatory treatment as referred to in Article 20 letter, it shall be carried out through: a. promotive efforts;
b. preventive efforts;
c. curative efforts; andd. rehabilitative efforts, in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

Article 53

Integrated services for Women victims of violence as referred to in Article 52 shall be implemented by adhering to principles, which include:
a. gender responsive;

non-discriminatory;

equal and respectful relations;

maintaining confidentiality;

providing a sense of security and comfort;
31- respecting individual differences;
f. non-judgmental;

respecting the choices and decisions of victims;

sensitive to the background and condition of victims and
i. use of language that is appropriate and understood by victims;

fast and simple;
k. empathy; and fulfillment of Women's rights. 1.

Article 178

Special Protection for Children victims of physical violence as referred to in Article 167 letter shall be carried out through efforts:
a. dissemination and socialization of provisions of laws and regulations that protect Children victims of acts of Violence;

monitoring,;

reporting; and imposition of sanctions.

Article 54

Forms of integrated services for Women victims of violence shall be provided in the form of:
a. complaint handling;

health rehabilitation;

social rehabilitation;

law enforcement and legal assistance; and repatriation and social reintegration.

Paragraph Complaint Handling

Article 67

Counseling services as referred to in Article 65 letter a aim to:
a. assist Women victims of violence in recognizing their problems and finding effective ways to overcome them independently;
b. empower Women victims of violence to determine their future;
c. provide moral support to Women victims of violence in facing the recovery process they are undergoing; and make Women victims of acts of violence feel accepted in the community environment.

Article 56

Complaints of acts of violence against Women may be made by reporters consisting of: victims;

family;

community; and/or community organizations engaged in the field of Women's protection.

