morality;

safety; and security.
(2) The Employer's Obligation to Women as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out by the Employer while the female worker is at the workplace and during the working hours that have been determined.

(3) Working hours as referred to in paragraph (2) apply to Women who enter into employment agreements for a definite period or for an indefinite period. Fixed-term employment agreements entered into by Employers and female workers, must be made in writing and must use the Indonesian language and Latin script.

(4) Fixed-term employment agreements entered into by Employers and female workers, must be made in writing and must use the Indonesian language and Latin script.

(5) Fixed-term employment agreements made by Employers and female workers may only be made for certain work which according to the type and nature or activity of the work will be completed within a certain time, namely as follows:

a. Work that is once completed or temporary in nature;
b. Work that is estimated to be completed within a not too long time;
c. Seasonal work;
d. Work related to new products, new activities, or additional products that are still in trial or exploration; or

e. Work whose type and nature or activity is not permanent.

(6) Fixed-term employment agreements made by Employers and female workers cannot be entered into for work that is permanent in nature.

(7) Fixed-term employment agreements that do not meet the provisions as referred to in paragraph (5) ir and paragraph (6) by law become indefinite-term employment agreements.

