Article 186

Strengthening and development of service provider institutions for Children requiring special protection as referred to in Article 166 letter shall be carried out through: a. capacity building of resources of service provider institutions for protection and handling of Children requiring special protection in the Region;
b. provision of specific needs for Children in special situations and conditions in the Region;
c. provision of communication, information, and education on protection of Children requiring special protection in the Region;
d. strengthening networks among service provider institutions for protection of Children requiring special protection in the Region; dane. facilitation of implementation of standardization of service provider institutions for protection of Children requiring special protection in the Region.

Article 139

The Regional Government is obliged to provide social welfare for:
a. b. Children in conflict with the law;

Children who are victims of violence who are exploited economically and sexually, Abandoned children, Children who are victims of kidnapping and Children who are victims of human trafficking;

Children who do not have parents and are cared for by parties or families who are unable;

Children who are victims of natural disasters or social disasters; and Children with disabilities.

Article 66

The provision of services as referred to in Article 65 shall be organized by
a. Regional Apparatus that organizes Government Affairs in the Social Sector;
b. Regional Apparatus that organizes Government Affairs in the Field of Women's Empowerment, and may cooperate with integrated service centers, women crisis centers or existing social community organizations;
c. Agencies; and/or
d. religious organizations.

Article 46

To anticipate and prevent acts of violence against Women, the Regional Government shall undertake the following efforts:
a. b. f. providing various public facilities suitable for Women in public spaces;

developing an integrated information system database on acts of violence against Women;

strengthening the competence of apparatus handling violence against Women;

creating various modules and guidelines on prevention and handling of acts of violence against Women;

conducting various trainings and guidance for social workers engaged in organizations/institutions handling violence against Women;

inviting the community to play an active role in recovery and reintegration;

strengthening the function of community organizations engaged in the field of Women's empowerment; conducting various socializations regarding prevention and anticipation of acts of violence against Women to various community components in the Region; and optimizing the role of religious institutions, customary institutions, culture, as well as exploring local wisdom in order to prevent and minimize violence against Women both occurring at home or outside the home.

Article 165

Strengthening and development of service provider institutions for improving the quality of life of Children as referred to in Article 163 letter is carried out through:

a. capacity building of resources of service provider institutions for improving the quality of life of Children in the Region;

b. assistance in implementing services for improving the quality of life of Children in the Region;

c. development of materials and implementation of Communication, Information, and Education on the fulfillment of Children's rights for service provider institutions for improving the quality of life of Children in the Region;

d. strengthening networks among service provider institutions for improving the quality of life of Children in the Region;

e. facilities for implementing standardization of service provider institutions for improving the quality of life of Children in the Region; and

f. development of service provider institutions for improving the quality of life of Children in the Region.

Article 164

The institutionalization of PHA as referred to in Article 163 letter is carried out through:

a. implementation of policies, programs and activities for the fulfillment of Children's rights in efforts to prevent violations of Children's rights in the Region;

b. increasing participation and the role of Children's forums or the like;

c. facilitating institutional strengthening and resources of government institutions, non-government institutions, the media, and the business sector;

d. facilitating the strengthening of networks among government institutions, non-government institutions, the media, and the business sector in the Region; and

e. strengthening cross-institutional cooperation among government institutions, non-government institutions, the media, and the business sector to realize KLA, Child-Friendly Sub-District (Kelana), Child-Friendly Village (Luna).

Paragraph Strengthening and Development of Service Provider Institutions for Improving the Quality of Life of Children.

Article 161

The Child-Friendly City Task Force as referred to in Article 158 has the main tasks: -61- coordinating the implementation of policies and

a. development of a Child-Friendly City;

b. conducting socialization, advocacy, and communication, information and education on Child-Friendly City policies;

c. collecting baseline data for the development of a Child-Friendly City;

d. conducting needs analysis based on baseline data;

e. disseminating baseline data;

f. determining the focus and priority of programs in realizing a Child-Friendly City, which is adjusted to regional potential;

g. preparing a (five)-year regional action plan for a Child-Friendly City and work mechanisms; and conducting monitoring, evaluation and reporting at least (once) a year.

